@*
    OdsExpandableCard — THE expand-in-place record card (Odyssey Design System ·
    ui_kits/web kit.css `.acct-list` / `.acct-item`).

    The dominant list UI in the client: Accounts, Contracts, Insurance policies, Tax
    statements, Subscriptions, Budgets, Journal entries and the analysis log all render
    their rows through this one component. A card head of four slots —
    Lead (type badge) · Head (name row + tag line) · Figures (right-hand headline) ·
    Actions (the row menu) — over an expandable Detail region.

    Its stylesheet is the GLOBAL `.acct-*` block in wwwroot/css/odyssey-components.css,
    not a scoped .razor.css. Every slot below is authored by the host page, so a scoped
    sheet would need `::deep` on nearly every selector — and, being bundled after the
    global sheets, would out-rank the page's own overrides. One sheet, one flash
    keyframe, one prefers-reduced-motion guard (issue #367).

    Keyboard: the `.acct-expand` <button> is the trigger and carries `aria-expanded` as a
    string (a bare bool renders nothing at all when false — issue #365). The head row's
    click is a redundant mouse affordance only, so it adds neither a second tab stop nor a
    nested interactive control.
*@

<div id="@Id" class="@RootClass">
    @* Mouse affordance: the whole head row toggles. Keyboard users operate the real
       expand <button> in the controls column. *@
    <div class="@HeadClass" @onclick="ToggleAsync">
        @Lead
        <div class="acct-id">@Head</div>
        @if (Figures is not null)
        {
            <div class="acct-figures">@Figures</div>
        }
        @* Clicks on the row menu (and anything else slotted here) must not toggle. *@
        <div class="acct-controls" @onclick:stopPropagation="true">
            @Actions
            <button type="button" class="acct-expand"
                    aria-expanded="@(Open ? "true" : "false")"
                    aria-label="@ToggleLabel"
                    @onclick="ToggleAsync">
                <span class="material-icons chev @(Open ? "open" : null)" aria-hidden="true">expand_more</span>
            </button>
        </div>
    </div>
    @if (Open && Detail is not null)
    {
        <div class="acct-detail">@Detail</div>
    }
</div>

@code {
    /// <summary>DOM id for the card — the jump-to-record target of a header problem rollup.</summary>
    [Parameter] public string? Id { get; set; }

    /// <summary>Whether the detail region is showing. Pair with OpenChanged / OnToggle.</summary>
    [Parameter] public bool Open { get; set; }

    [Parameter] public EventCallback<bool> OpenChanged { get; set; }

    /// <summary>Fires with the next open state on head or trigger activation.</summary>
    [Parameter] public EventCallback<bool> OnToggle { get; set; }

    /// <summary>The record has left the working set (archived / closed) — dims the type badge.</summary>
    [Parameter] public bool Dimmed { get; set; }

    /// <summary>One-shot attention ring, for when a header rollup jumps to this record.</summary>
    [Parameter] public bool Flash { get; set; }

    /// <summary>The record's name — becomes the trigger's accessible name
    /// ("Expand Everyday checking"). Omit for a bare "Expand" / "Collapse".</summary>
    [Parameter] public string? Label { get; set; }

    /// <summary>Top-align the head columns instead of centring them — for a multi-line
    /// head (the Journal card's snippet + tag chips).</summary>
    [Parameter] public bool AlignTop { get; set; }

    /// <summary>Extra CSS class(es) appended to the root (e.g. a page-specific modifier).</summary>
    [Parameter] public string? Class { get; set; }

    /// <summary>The leading cell — conventionally a <c>.acct-badge</c> type icon.</summary>
    [Parameter] public RenderFragment? Lead { get; set; }

    /// <summary>The identity column: the <c>.acct-name-row</c> and the <c>.acct-tags</c> sub-line.</summary>
    [Parameter, EditorRequired] public RenderFragment? Head { get; set; }

    /// <summary>The right-hand headline figure + caption. Omit for a three-column head.</summary>
    [Parameter] public RenderFragment? Figures { get; set; }

    /// <summary>Row controls (the overflow menu), placed left of the expand trigger.
    /// Clicks here never toggle the card.</summary>
    [Parameter] public RenderFragment? Actions { get; set; }

    /// <summary>The expanded detail region — rendered only while <see cref="Open"/>.</summary>
    [Parameter] public RenderFragment? Detail { get; set; }

    private string RootClass =>
        $"acct-item{(Open ? " open" : null)}{(Dimmed ? " dimmed" : null)}{(Flash ? " flash" : null)}{(string.IsNullOrWhiteSpace(Class) ? null : $" {Class}")}";

    private string HeadClass =>
        $"acct-head{(Figures is null ? " no-figures" : null)}{(AlignTop ? " align-top" : null)}";

    private string ToggleLabel =>
        string.IsNullOrWhiteSpace(Label)
            ? (Open ? "Collapse" : "Expand")
            : $"{(Open ? "Collapse" : "Expand")} {Label}";

    private async Task ToggleAsync()
    {
        var next = !Open;
        await OpenChanged.InvokeAsync(next);
        await OnToggle.InvokeAsync(next);
    }
}
